    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0292" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg250"/>

                <head>Lord Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 9, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of this day’s date, requesting to be informed whether the means
                    thus far adopted or intended on the part of her Majesty’s government in the case
                    of the Alexandra would be in any way deranged by simultaneous action on the part
                    of the United States in a different form, and I beg to state to you that I have
                    referred a copy of your letter to the lords commissioners of her Majesty’s
                    treasury, and as soon as I receive their lordships’ reply I shall have the honor
                    of making a further communication to you on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
